<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Junius Brutus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">85–42 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Junius Brutus was a Roman senator who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-cassius-longinus">Gaius Cassius Longinus</a>, led the conspiracy that killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> on the Ides of March 44 BCE. Claiming to defend the Republic, he left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and raised forces in the eastern provinces. After his defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Octavian at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi">Battle of Philippi</a> in 42 BCE, he took his own life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-junius-brutus.jpg" alt="Marcus Junius Brutus" width="250" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brutusidesobv.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
